  "difficulty": 2,
  "module_type": "standard",
  "question_text": "In the xy-plane, the circle shown has equation (x - 3)^2 + (y + 2)^2 = 100, and point P(9, 6) lies on the circle. Line t is tangent to the circle at P. What is the x-coordinate of the x-intercept of line t?",
  "answer_a": "1",
  "answer_b": "4.5",
  "answer_c": "13.5",
  "answer_d": "17",
  "correct_answer": "D",
  "explanation": "Choice D is correct. The equation of the circle is (x - 3)^2 + (y + 2)^2 = 100, so the center of the circle is C(3, -2). The radius CP has slope (6 - (-2))/(9 - 3) = 8/6 = 4/3. A tangent line is perpendicular to the radius at the point of tangency, so the slope of line t is the negative reciprocal of 4/3, which is -3/4. Line t passes through P(9, 6), so its equation is y - 6 = -(3/4)(x - 9). At the x-intercept, y = 0, so -6 = -(3/4)(x - 9). Multiplying each side by -4/3 gives 8 = x - 9, so x = 17. Therefore, the x-coordinate of the x-intercept of line t is 17.",
  "distractor_a_explanation": "Choice A is incorrect. This results from taking the reciprocal of the radius slope but not changing its sign, so the slope used for line t is 3/4 instead of -3/4. Then 0 - 6 = (3/4)(x - 9) gives x - 9 = -8, so x = 1.",
  "distractor_b_explanation": "Choice B is incorrect. This results from using the slope of the radius, 4/3, as the slope of line t, which makes line t parallel to the radius rather than perpendicular to it. Then 0 - 6 = (4/3)(x - 9) gives x - 9 = -4.5, so x = 4.5.",
  "distractor_c_explanation": "Choice C is incorrect. This results from changing the sign of the radius slope but not taking the reciprocal, so the slope used for line t is -4/3 instead of -3/4. Then 0 - 6 = -(4/3)(x - 9) gives x - 9 = 4.5, so x = 13.5.",
  "distractor_d_explanation": "",
