 {
  "section": "math",
  "skill_category": "Geometry and Trigonometry",
  "skill_subcategory": "Circles",
  "difficulty": 2,
  "module_type": "standard",
  "question_text": "In the figure shown, points A, B, and C lie on a circle with center O and diameter 30 centimeters. Point C lies on the major arc AB. The measure of central angle AOB is (9x + 12) degrees, and the measure of inscribed angle ACB is (4x + 12) degrees. What is the length, in centimeters, of minor arc AB?",
  "answer_a": "5π",
  "answer_b": "10π",
  "answer_c": "20π",
  "answer_d": "30π",
  "correct_answer": "B",
  "explanation": "Choice B is correct. Central angle AOB and inscribed angle ACB intercept the same arc AB, so the central angle is twice the inscribed angle. Therefore, 9x + 12 = 2(4x + 12), which simplifies to 9x + 12 = 8x + 24, so x = 12. The measure of central angle AOB is 9(12) + 12 = 120 degrees, which is 120/360 = 1/3 of a full rotation. The diameter is 30 centimeters, so the radius is 15 centimeters and the circumference is 2π(15) = 30π centimeters. Therefore, the length of minor arc AB is (1/3)(30π) = 10π centimeters.",
  "distractor_a_explanation": "Choice A is incorrect. This results from using the inscribed angle, 4(12) + 12 = 60 degrees, as the arc's angle instead of the central angle: (60/360)(30π) = 5π.",
  "distractor_b_explanation": "",
  "distractor_c_explanation": "Choice C is incorrect. This results from treating the diameter, 30 centimeters, as the radius, so the circumference is computed as 2π(30) = 60π and the arc is (120/360)(60π) = 20π.",
  "distractor_d_explanation": "Choice D is incorrect. This is the circumference of the entire circle, 2π(15) = 30π, not the length of arc AB; it results from forgetting to multiply by the fraction 120/360 of the circle.",
  "is_diagnostic": false,
  "is_active": true,
  "has_visual": true,
